<item><title>Algeria issues orange rain alerts for 22 wilayas</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/algeria-issues-orange-rain-alerts-for-22-wilayas-2adb02/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/algeria-issues-orange-rain-alerts-for-22-wilayas-2adb02/</guid><category>Algeria</category><description>The meteorological office forecasts 20 to 40 mm in some areas, after farmers raised concern over a lack of rain during ploughing.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:10:52 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dz.jpg" length="32980" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dz.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Attaf denies Algeria ordered a boycott of French goods</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/attaf-denies-algeria-ordered-a-boycott-of-french-goods-393088/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/attaf-denies-algeria-ordered-a-boycott-of-french-goods-393088/</guid><category>Algeria</category><description>The foreign minister said French suppliers lost ground on price and competition, and urged Paris to use the EU-Algeria Association Council to discuss the dispute.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:45:36 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/attaf-denies-algeria-ordered-a-boycott-of-french-goods-393088/share.jpg" length="41980" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/attaf-denies-algeria-ordered-a-boycott-of-french-goods-393088/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Algerian army seizes more than a million pregabalin tablets in In Salah</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/algerian-army-seizes-more-than-a-million-pregabalin-tablets-a24341/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/algerian-army-seizes-more-than-a-million-pregabalin-tablets-a24341/</guid><category>Algeria</category><description>The army said two traffickers were killed on Wednesday, 25 November, after refusing orders to stop while trying to bring the tablets into Algeria.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:35:04 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dz.jpg" length="32980" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dz.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
